[Engines whooshing]

1552
01:01:09,333 --> 01:01:13,437
Jet traffic.

1553
01:01:13,470 --> 01:01:15,407
Say...

1554
01:01:15,440 --> 01:01:17,642
We have preserved this huge
diamond in our village

1555
01:01:17,675 --> 01:01:18,843
for many generations.

1556
01:01:18,877 --> 01:01:21,478
But what has the diamond
got to do with barugon?

1557
01:01:21,512 --> 01:01:23,782
Ah, keep your shirt on.
It's cubic zirconia.

1558
01:01:23,815 --> 01:01:27,318
This'll draw him on
irresistibly.

1559
01:01:27,352 --> 01:01:30,053
We can use it
to lure him into the water?

1560
01:01:30,087 --> 01:01:31,855
Does your village have many
diamonds this size?

1561
01:01:31,888 --> 01:01:34,492
Simmer down,
you gold digger. Gee.

1562
01:01:34,525 --> 01:01:36,160
Just this one is left.

1563
01:01:36,193 --> 01:01:38,963
Every thousand years
a monster such as this

1564
01:01:38,997 --> 01:01:40,330
is born in my village.

1565
01:01:40,363 --> 01:01:41,332
That's a long
gestation period.

1566
01:01:41,365 --> 01:01:42,567
Each time one is born,

1567
01:01:42,600 --> 01:01:44,735
another of our diamonds
must be sacrificed.

1568
01:01:44,768 --> 01:01:45,970
It is dropped into the lake

1569
01:01:46,003 --> 01:01:47,972
to lure the monster
to its death.

1570
01:01:48,005 --> 01:01:49,673
If that's the case,
I realize how precious

1571
01:01:49,707 --> 01:01:51,208
this last diamond is.

1572
01:01:51,242 --> 01:01:53,610
Are you sure
that barugon will respond

1573
01:01:53,643 --> 01:01:55,145
as the legend has predicted?

1574
01:01:55,178 --> 01:01:56,847
If you don't believe in it,

1575
01:01:56,880 --> 01:01:58,548
you are doubting the gods.

1576
01:01:58,582 --> 01:02:00,885
Whoa. Guess I stepped on
a few toes there.

1577
01:02:00,918 --> 01:02:01,918
Sorry.

1578
01:02:01,952 --> 01:02:03,320
We haven't time to waste.

1579
01:02:03,353 --> 01:02:05,457
It's the only idea
that hasn't been tried.

1580
01:02:05,490 --> 01:02:06,757
Oh, what about the "z" plan?

1581
01:02:06,790 --> 01:02:08,192
We'll put it to work at once.

1582
01:02:08,225 --> 01:02:09,293
Sorry.

1583
01:02:09,293 --> 01:02:11,262
In which direction
shall we guide you?

1584
01:02:11,295 --> 01:02:14,398
Is there a large lake
to sink him in?

1585
01:02:14,432 --> 01:02:17,000
There's biwa lake.

1586
01:02:17,033 --> 01:02:18,102
I can't untie it.

1587
01:02:18,135 --> 01:02:19,537
Well, cut it with that knife.
There.

1588
01:02:19,570 --> 01:02:22,173
Geishas who love too much.

1589
01:02:22,207 --> 01:02:23,842
Hurry.

1590
01:02:23,875 --> 01:02:25,743
Oh, the rope,
not my wrist.

1591
01:02:25,777 --> 01:02:26,877
Careful.

1592
01:02:26,910 --> 01:02:28,678
...the safest place
to deposit him.

1593
01:02:28,712 --> 01:02:31,282
Authorities hope
that the 5,000 karat diamond...

1594
01:02:31,315 --> 01:02:33,750
That's it. Talk it over
with jack daniels.

1595
01:02:33,785 --> 01:02:35,820
Wow.
What an incredible scheme.

1596
01:02:35,853 --> 01:02:37,388
A 5,000 karat diamond,

1597
01:02:37,422 --> 01:02:39,990
to be sunk in biwa lake,
just to get the monster.

1598
01:02:40,023 --> 01:02:41,025
What?

1599
01:02:41,058 --> 01:02:42,460
Are you sure?

1600
01:02:42,527 --> 01:02:45,328
Of course. A native girl
brought it to japan.

1601
01:02:45,362 --> 01:02:46,563
Who told you?

1602
01:02:46,597 --> 01:02:47,698
The radio announced it.

1603
01:02:47,732 --> 01:02:49,767
Was she in
bride of frankenstein?

1604
01:02:53,805 --> 01:02:55,607
Those natives
did have a jewel.

1605
01:02:55,640 --> 01:02:58,708
Worth more
than I'd ever dreamed of.

1606
01:02:58,742 --> 01:03:00,478
But daddy needs his medicine.

1607
01:03:00,512 --> 01:03:02,147
Ah.

1608
01:03:02,180 --> 01:03:03,680
Last call.

1609
01:03:03,713 --> 01:03:06,617
All right.
So I'll get it.

1610
01:03:06,650 --> 01:03:09,320
Want a drool bucket?
Oh, right on me.

1611
01:03:09,353 --> 01:03:13,190
In a final attempt
to rid japan of barugon,

1612
01:03:13,223 --> 01:03:15,258
operation diamond
is put into effect.

1613
01:03:15,292 --> 01:03:16,660
They offered him a cocktail.

1614
01:03:16,660 --> 01:03:18,128
A 5,000 karat diamond
is used

1615
01:03:18,162 --> 01:03:19,363
to trick the monster

1616
01:03:19,397 --> 01:03:22,132
into abandoning
his natural environment, land,

1617
01:03:22,167 --> 01:03:24,068
for the waters of lake biwa.

1618
01:03:24,102 --> 01:03:28,205
Scenic lake biwa.

1619
01:03:28,238 --> 01:03:30,608
Yeah, right.
I'm heading off to a lake?

1620
01:03:30,642 --> 01:03:32,243
You think
I was born yesterday?

1621
01:03:32,277 --> 01:03:34,712
Oh, wait. I was.

1622
01:03:34,745 --> 01:03:36,513
Traffic on the i-94 outbound

1623
01:03:36,547 --> 01:03:37,548
is still bumper to bumper

1624
01:03:37,582 --> 01:03:39,417
during the sundown slowdown.

1625
01:03:44,555 --> 01:03:46,323
[Roars]

1626
01:03:46,357 --> 01:03:48,025
Want it.

1627
01:03:50,327 --> 01:03:53,230
Barugon, are you up to one
of your little schemes again,

1628
01:03:53,263 --> 01:03:56,800
you little conniver?

1629
01:03:56,833 --> 01:03:58,402
Get me.
I'm carol channing.

1630
01:03:58,435 --> 01:04:00,003
No, he's cuter
than carol channing.

1631
01:04:00,037 --> 01:04:02,973
Oh.

1632
01:04:03,007 --> 01:04:04,775
You know,
don't you think a disco ball

1633
01:04:04,808 --> 01:04:06,143
would have been
a little cheaper?

1634
01:04:06,177 --> 01:04:09,313
Mm-hmm.

1635
01:04:09,347 --> 01:04:10,715
Oh, look.
There's liz taylor.

1636
01:04:10,748 --> 01:04:12,048
No, he's smaller
than liz taylor.

1637
01:04:12,082 --> 01:04:13,517
Come on. Be nice.

1638
01:04:13,550 --> 01:04:15,687
Oh, fun.

1639
01:04:17,455 --> 01:04:18,455
What's wrong?

1640
01:04:18,488 --> 01:04:19,823
Keep dangling
and shaking it.

1641
01:04:19,857 --> 01:04:21,725
I think he's going for it.

1642
01:04:21,758 --> 01:04:23,962
Try jerk bait.

1643
01:04:26,830 --> 01:04:28,732
I--i gotta go walkies.

1644
01:04:28,765 --> 01:04:30,467
Ugh.

1645
01:04:33,905 --> 01:04:36,540
No use.
He won't follow.

1646
01:04:36,573 --> 01:04:39,977
We've failed.

1647
01:04:40,010 --> 01:04:41,445
Here's one for you.

1648
01:04:41,478 --> 01:04:42,680
Why did I cross the road?

1649
01:04:42,713 --> 01:04:44,715
There's no right answer.
I don't even know.

1650
01:04:44,748 --> 01:04:46,183
[Laughter]

1651
01:04:46,217 --> 01:04:47,918
Now what?

1652
01:04:47,952 --> 01:04:51,088
We smell one.

1653
01:04:51,122 --> 01:04:52,623
Shame, shame, all around.

1654
01:04:52,657 --> 01:04:54,292
I don't understand.

1655
01:04:59,430 --> 01:05:02,065
Overpass?
I don't think so.

1656
01:05:10,742 --> 01:05:12,242
If this legend
that the villagers believe in

1657
01:05:12,277 --> 01:05:13,543
- is really true...
- And I doubt it.

1658
01:05:13,577 --> 01:05:16,613
Then kindly tell me why
he disregarded the diamond.

1659
01:05:16,647 --> 01:05:18,182
He didn't like the cut,
the clarity,

1660
01:05:18,215 --> 01:05:19,250
the color, or karat.

1661
01:05:19,283 --> 01:05:20,685
I suspected the validity
of her story

1662
01:05:20,718 --> 01:05:22,520
from the first time
that I heard her speak.

1663
01:05:22,553 --> 01:05:23,955
It was too much
of a fairytale

1664
01:05:23,988 --> 01:05:25,455
and we should never
have listened to her.

1665
01:05:25,488 --> 01:05:27,023
Aw, jeez,
heap more shame on her.

1666
01:05:27,057 --> 01:05:29,460
Besides, I doubt very much
that there was a real diamond.

1667
01:05:29,527 --> 01:05:31,528
If a gem that size
existed anywhere in the world,

1668
01:05:31,562 --> 01:05:32,930
there'd be reports of it.

1669
01:05:32,963 --> 01:05:35,565
So it failed.
But it isn't her fault.

1670
01:05:35,598 --> 01:05:37,735
She was doing her best
to give you her help.

1671
01:05:37,768 --> 01:05:39,970
- Listen.
- You're just trying to lay
all the blame on us.

1672
01:05:40,003 --> 01:05:41,905
[All]
Yeah, and scarecrow's brain!

1673
01:05:41,938 --> 01:05:43,340
Just remember
that it was your greed

1674
01:05:43,373 --> 01:05:45,475
that brought all this misery
upon us in the first place.

1675
01:05:45,508 --> 01:05:46,510
You got me.

1676
01:05:46,543 --> 01:05:48,045
But still.
We tried to help.

1677
01:05:48,078 --> 01:05:49,347
Be quiet!

1678
01:05:49,380 --> 01:05:50,580
And go to your room.

1679
01:05:50,613 --> 01:05:52,550
I acted shamefully,
I know.

1680
01:05:52,583 --> 01:05:54,218
She's blameless.

1681
01:05:54,252 --> 01:05:56,153
She gave you one possible plan.

1682
01:05:56,187 --> 01:05:59,323
It's just been a foolish
waste of precious time.

1683
01:05:59,357 --> 01:06:00,992
I know,
but it isn't her fault.

1684
01:06:01,025 --> 01:06:02,860
Die! Die! Die!

1685
01:06:02,860 --> 01:06:06,563
I'm sorry. Forgive me.

1686
01:06:06,597 --> 01:06:10,500
Areas to the west
have been moved...

1687
01:06:10,533 --> 01:06:11,735
I have to go now.

1688
01:06:11,768 --> 01:06:14,905
To the little
general's room, you know.

1689
01:06:14,938 --> 01:06:18,908
He hurts me so.

1690
01:06:18,942 --> 01:06:20,177
There, there, dear.

1691
01:06:20,210 --> 01:06:22,145
Let's get you a pint
of fresh type "a."

1692
01:06:25,515 --> 01:06:27,985
Hmm?

1693
01:06:28,018 --> 01:06:29,220
Oh, get a room.

1694
01:06:29,253 --> 01:06:30,855
Mm-hmm.

1695
01:06:30,888 --> 01:06:32,890
I'll repeat that message...

1696
01:06:32,923 --> 01:06:34,858
Uh, I hate to pull rank
on you, son,

1697
01:06:34,892 --> 01:06:35,927
but, uh, hmm.

1698
01:06:35,993 --> 01:06:37,895
In fact, we're very much
obliged to you.

1699
01:06:37,928 --> 01:06:40,097
You tried your best.

1700
01:06:40,130 --> 01:06:42,533
She is a wild tigress,
isn't she?

1701
01:06:42,567 --> 01:06:44,835
Excuse me.
This gentleman is dr. Sato.

1702
01:06:44,868 --> 01:06:45,870
Hello.

1703
01:06:45,903 --> 01:06:47,303
Ah. How are you?

1704
01:06:47,337 --> 01:06:48,905
- Fine, thanks.
- Good.

1705
01:06:48,938 --> 01:06:50,073
You?

1706
01:06:50,107 --> 01:06:51,242
This time you've got
some real trouble.

1707
01:06:51,275 --> 01:06:53,143
Oh, we certainly have.

1708
01:06:53,177 --> 01:06:54,378
Think you can help us?

1709
01:06:54,412 --> 01:06:55,913
Have you got some
suggestions to make?

1710
01:06:55,947 --> 01:06:58,548
I'm glad I stopped by.
On my way over here...

1711
01:06:58,582 --> 01:07:00,083
I believe that barugon

1712
01:07:00,117 --> 01:07:03,087
was exposed to an infrared ray
while still an egg.

1713
01:07:03,120 --> 01:07:05,588
And I believe for every
drop of rain that falls

1714
01:07:05,622 --> 01:07:06,590
a flower grows.

1715
01:07:06,623 --> 01:07:07,958
You see,
I was on the ship

1716
01:07:07,992 --> 01:07:09,627
that brought the egg
here to japan.

1717
01:07:09,660 --> 01:07:11,928
Onodera. He was the man
who found the egg,

1718
01:07:11,962 --> 01:07:13,597
thinking it was a gem.

1719
01:07:13,630 --> 01:07:15,933
He was then receiving
infrared-ray treatment

1720
01:07:15,967 --> 01:07:16,967
for athlete's foot.

1721
01:07:17,000 --> 01:07:18,202
What's so absorbing, junior?

1722
01:07:18,235 --> 01:07:19,437
Now it seems quite possible

1723
01:07:19,470 --> 01:07:20,938
that he forgot
to turn the lamp off.

1724
01:07:20,972 --> 01:07:23,673
It was probably directed
towards the egg.

1725
01:07:23,707 --> 01:07:25,542
Hey, look back there.

1726
01:07:25,575 --> 01:07:28,145
It's cary grant
in the faberge years.

1727
01:07:28,178 --> 01:07:29,280
At very close range,

1728
01:07:29,313 --> 01:07:31,248
and over quite a substantial
period of time.

1729
01:07:31,282 --> 01:07:32,983
Castro's there too.

1730
01:07:33,017 --> 01:07:36,120
...speeded up considerably
the growth of the monster.

1731
01:07:36,153 --> 01:07:37,688
Then that explains it.

1732
01:07:37,722 --> 01:07:39,990
Now I understand
what's happened.

1733
01:07:40,023 --> 01:07:42,358
The legend says barugon
should take ten years

1734
01:07:42,392 --> 01:07:43,593
to reach his present size.

1735
01:07:43,593 --> 01:07:45,128
Ah, indeed.

1736
01:07:45,162 --> 01:07:48,265
Are you certain that it should
take ten years to mature?

1737
01:07:48,298 --> 01:07:49,767
Yes. I am.

1738
01:07:49,800 --> 01:07:52,603
Barugon is really a freak
with an abnormal body.

1739
01:07:52,637 --> 01:07:53,703
I know the feeling.

1740
01:07:53,737 --> 01:07:55,907
That's something
we doctors can explain.

1741
01:07:55,940 --> 01:07:59,310
If an expectant mother
is exposed to radioactivity,

1742
01:07:59,343 --> 01:08:00,310
a freak may be born.

1743
01:08:00,343 --> 01:08:01,812
Like rick james?

1744
01:08:01,845 --> 01:08:05,015
So then that's why it showed
no interest in the diamond.

1745
01:08:05,048 --> 01:08:06,050
That's right.

1746
01:08:06,083 --> 01:08:07,918
He's a super freak.

1747
01:08:07,952 --> 01:08:10,855
Listen. Now that we know
that it's a freak,

1748
01:08:10,888 --> 01:08:13,290
isn't there some different way
that we should attack it?

1749
01:08:13,323 --> 01:08:14,892
It's herbie!

1750
01:08:14,925 --> 01:08:17,327
Expose the diamond
to the infrared ray.

1751
01:08:17,327 --> 01:08:18,762
Will that do us any good?

1752
01:08:18,795 --> 01:08:22,365
No, but it will
pad the film out a little bit.

1753
01:08:22,398 --> 01:08:25,235
...barugon must therefore
respond favorably to it.

1754
01:08:25,268 --> 01:08:27,538
Yeah, I'm buying this
big time.

1755
01:08:27,572 --> 01:08:31,108
Now then. Perhaps the diamond,
if radioactive,

1756
01:08:31,142 --> 01:08:32,142
will be effective.

1757
01:08:32,175 --> 01:08:34,010
Barugon may respond to it

1758
01:08:34,043 --> 01:08:35,145
as you first hoped.

1759
01:08:35,178 --> 01:08:36,547
Barugon, that's me.

1760
01:08:36,580 --> 01:08:39,717
Karen, is there any way to make
him stay where he is now?

1761
01:08:39,750 --> 01:08:41,218
Uh, we could staple him
to the floor.

1762
01:08:41,252 --> 01:08:42,418
There's one possibility.

1763
01:08:42,452 --> 01:08:45,055
Our villages have all
been praying for rain.

1764
01:08:45,088 --> 01:08:47,925
If heaven cares,
it will send us rain.

1765
01:08:47,958 --> 01:08:48,958
Why rain?

1766
01:08:48,992 --> 01:08:50,160
You got a better idea?

1767
01:08:50,193 --> 01:08:51,562
Water will weaken him.

1768
01:08:51,595 --> 01:08:55,232
Our legend says that the monster
cannot move while it rains.

1769
01:08:55,265 --> 01:08:57,300
She kiddin' us?

1770
01:08:57,333 --> 01:08:59,270
But why wait for the gods.

1771
01:08:59,303 --> 01:09:02,172
Isn't it easy now
to create rain?

1772
01:09:02,205 --> 01:09:03,640
Heck, my aunt could do it.

1773
01:09:03,673 --> 01:09:05,108
We'll produce it, all right.

1774
01:09:05,142 --> 01:09:06,143
You direct.

1775
01:09:06,177 --> 01:09:09,413
Manmade rain
from helicopters.

1776
01:09:09,447 --> 01:09:11,848
A flight of helicopters
is sent to fly over barugon...

1777
01:09:11,882 --> 01:09:13,017
[Coughing]

1778
01:09:13,050 --> 01:09:15,218
...spraying onto him
manmade rain.

1779
01:09:15,252 --> 01:09:17,722
A mist-like liquid,
which it is hoped,

1780
01:09:17,755 --> 01:09:19,723
will arrest
the monster's movements.

1781
01:09:19,757 --> 01:09:21,458
Send in the clouds.

1782
01:09:21,492 --> 01:09:22,693
The rain should make barugon

1783
01:09:22,727 --> 01:09:24,562
unable to exhale
his freezing vapor,

1784
01:09:24,595 --> 01:09:26,563
thus rendering him harmless.

1785
01:09:26,597 --> 01:09:27,665
Or at least drowsy

1786
01:09:27,698 --> 01:09:29,733
and unable to operate
heavy machinery.

1787
01:09:33,837 --> 01:09:35,472
[With british accent]
Well, could be worse.

1788
01:09:35,505 --> 01:09:36,473
How?

1789
01:09:36,507 --> 01:09:37,507
Could be rainin'.

1790
01:09:37,542 --> 01:09:39,710
Whoa.

1791
01:09:39,743 --> 01:09:44,080
Catch the drops on your tongue.
It's fun.

1792
01:09:44,113 --> 01:09:48,352
You know, uh, rainy days
and mondays always get me down.

1793
01:09:48,385 --> 01:09:49,387
It's true.

1794
01:09:49,420 --> 01:09:53,623
Poppies.
Poppies will make him sleep.

1795
01:09:53,657 --> 01:09:55,592
Well, let's head over
to the bozo drum!

1796
01:09:55,625 --> 01:09:56,760
Hoo-hoo!

1797
01:09:56,827 --> 01:09:58,728
This machine is called
a death ray projector,

1798
01:09:58,762 --> 01:10:01,832
and a ruby is put in
to act upon the light molecules.

1799
01:10:01,865 --> 01:10:05,202
Thus the waves of light
are broken down.

1800
01:10:05,235 --> 01:10:07,037
- Right now...
- Oh, just get on with it.

1801
01:10:07,070 --> 01:10:09,038
You can see the machine
is in the experimental stage,

1802
01:10:09,072 --> 01:10:11,442
and cannot be put
to practical use.

1803
01:10:11,475 --> 01:10:15,478
But now possibly
we can employ the diamond

1804
01:10:15,512 --> 01:10:16,513
- instead of the ruby.
- Neat.

1805
01:10:16,547 --> 01:10:18,848
- Let's insert it.
- Together.

1806
